"""Give the weather service a way to be configured.

weather_service.c reads weather.key / weather.city from the config store, but
nothing could write them: this CLI has no generic "set <key> <value>", only a
purpose-built set_* per setting. So the service shipped unconfigurable -- it
would idle forever with "no weather.key configured" and no route out.

One command takes both values, since a key with no city is useless (the AMap
endpoint rejects a request without city) and asking for two commands to get one
feature working is a trap.
